    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d929">

                <pb facs="0870" n="860" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg860"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/2481: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-26T12:00:00+09:00">April 26,
                            1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your [<hi rendition="#italic">Chungking’s</hi>] April 25, 11 a.m.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d929-f1"/> I have notified Senior Consul today in writing that the
                    Government of the United States consents to the establishment of the provisional
                    council under the terms of resolution number 4. Several other governments,
                    including the British, Japanese and German, have also communicated their
                    consent.</p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking. Repeated to the Department and Peiping. Code text by air mail
                    to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
